#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "A unified suite of desktop micro-utilities for Linux"
msgstr "适用于 Linux 的桌面小工具合集"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Everyday desktop micro-utilities for Linux, in one binary.\n"
"\n"
"Run without a subcommand to open the GTK control center. Each subcommand runs one utility from the terminal, a script or a keyboard shortcut."
msgstr ""
"适用于 Linux 的日常桌面小工具，集于一个程序。\n"
"\n"
"不带子命令运行即可打开 GTK 控制中心。每个子命令可在终端、脚本或键盘快捷键中运行一个工具。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard"
msgstr "选取屏幕区域，并将识别出的文字复制到剪贴板"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard\n"
"\n"
"Opens the desktop's interactive screenshot tool through the XDG Screenshot portal, then runs Tesseract on the selected region. Without the portal it falls back to grim+slurp, gnome-screenshot, spectacle or maim. The text is printed and copied to the clipboard."
msgstr ""
"选取屏幕区域，并将识别出的文字复制到剪贴板\n"
"\n"
"通过 XDG Screenshot 门户打开桌面的交互式截图工具，然后对所选区域运行 Tesseract。没有该门户时，会改用 grim+slurp、gnome-screenshot、spectacle 或 maim。文字会被打印出来并复制到剪贴板。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Tesseract language code(s), e.g. \"eng\" or \"eng+deu\""
msgstr "Tesseract 语言代码，例如 \"eng\" 或 \"eng+deu\""

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value"
msgstr "从屏幕取色并复制其 HEX 值"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Pick a color from the screen and copy its HEX value\n"
"\n"
"Uses the XDG Screenshot portal's color picker. The value is printed, copied to the clipboard and added to the color history shown in the control center."
msgstr ""
"从屏幕取色并复制其 HEX 值\n"
"\n"
"使用 XDG Screenshot 门户的取色器。该值会被打印出来、复制到剪贴板，并加入控制中心中显示的颜色历史。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast"
msgstr "转换颜色（#hex 或 rgb(...)）并报告 WCAG 对比度"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Convert a color (#hex or rgb(...)) and report WCAG contrast\n"
"\n"
"Prints the color as HEX, RGB and HSL, and its WCAG 2.x contrast ratio as text on white and on black."
msgstr ""
"转换颜色（#hex 或 rgb(...)）并报告 WCAG 对比度\n"
"\n"
"以 HEX、RGB 和 HSL 打印该颜色，并给出它作为文字分别放在白底和黑底上的 WCAG 2.x 对比度。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "#rgb, #rrggbb (the # is optional) or rgb(r, g, b)"
msgstr "#rgb、#rrggbb（# 可省略）或 rgb(r, g, b)"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files"
msgstr "删除元数据并压缩 PNG、JPEG、WebP 或 MP4 文件"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files\n"
"\n"
"Each FILE is written to NAME.min.EXT beside it; originals are never modified."
msgstr ""
"删除元数据并压缩 PNG、JPEG、WebP 或 MP4 文件\n"
"\n"
"每个 FILE 都会写入它旁边的 NAME.min.EXT；原文件绝不会被修改。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Files to compress (.png, .jpg/.jpeg, .webp, .mp4/.m4v/.mov)"
msgstr "要压缩的文件（.png、.jpg/.jpeg、.webp、.mp4/.m4v/.mov）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Quality from 1 (smallest) to 100 (best); ignored for PNG, which is always lossless"
msgstr "质量，从 1（最小）到 100（最佳）；对始终无损的 PNG 无效"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Expand a snippet template, e.g. \"Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}\""
msgstr "展开片段模板，例如 \"Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}\""

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Expand a snippet template, e.g. \"Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}\"\n"
"\n"
"Prints TEMPLATE with its {variables} replaced. Fails if a variable is unknown or an {arg:NAME} has no matching --arg."
msgstr ""
"展开片段模板，例如 \"Sent {date:%A}: {clipboard}\"\n"
"\n"
"打印 TEMPLATE，并将其中的 {variables} 替换掉。如果有未知变量，或某个 {arg:NAME} 没有对应的 --arg，则会失败。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Text with {variables} to expand; quote it to keep the braces from the shell"
msgstr "包含要展开的 {variables} 的文本；请加引号，避免 shell 处理花括号"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "A value for {arg:NAME}; repeat for several parameters"
msgstr "{arg:NAME} 的值；有多个参数时重复使用"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app"
msgstr "打开片段选择器，并将所选片段粘贴到当前焦点所在的应用"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Open the snippet picker and paste the chosen snippet into the focused app\n"
"\n"
"Search with the keyboard, press Enter, and fill in any {arg:NAME} parameters. The expansion is pasted into the app that had focus, through the RemoteDesktop portal (the desktop asks for permission once), and the previous clipboard is restored."
msgstr ""
"打开片段选择器，并将所选片段粘贴到当前焦点所在的应用\n"
"\n"
"用键盘搜索，按 Enter，并填写所有 {arg:NAME} 参数。展开的内容会通过 RemoteDesktop 门户粘贴到原先有焦点的应用（桌面只会请求一次权限），之前的剪贴板内容会被恢复。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Open directly on the snippet with this trigger"
msgstr "直接打开具有此触发词的片段"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Set up and toggle typed triggers (type ;date anywhere to expand it)"
msgstr "设置并切换键入触发词（在任何地方键入 ;date 即可展开）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Set up and toggle typed triggers (type ;date anywhere to expand it)\n"
"\n"
"Typed triggers read keyboard input through evdev and paste through a uinput virtual keyboard, which needs a one-time setup with root rights. Only the last few typed characters are kept in memory; nothing is logged or stored."
msgstr ""
"设置并切换键入触发词（在任何地方键入 ;date 即可展开）\n"
"\n"
"键入触发词通过 evdev 读取键盘输入，并通过 uinput 虚拟键盘粘贴，这需要用 root 权限进行一次性设置。内存中只保留最近键入的几个字符；不会记录或存储任何内容。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show whether typed triggers are enabled and can run"
msgstr "显示键入触发词是否已开启并能正常运行"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Grant keyboard access and turn typed triggers on, right away (no logout needed)"
msgstr "授予键盘访问权限并立即开启键入触发词（无需注销）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Run the commands (asks for the administrator password) instead of only printing them"
msgstr "运行这些命令（会要求输入管理员密码），而不只是打印它们"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Turn typed triggers on"
msgstr "开启键入触发词"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Turn typed triggers off"
msgstr "关闭键入触发词"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Turn typed triggers off and remove Voltkit's keyboard access"
msgstr "关闭键入触发词并移除 Voltkit 的键盘访问权限"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Measure distances on screen in pixels"
msgstr "以像素为单位测量屏幕上的距离"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Measure distances on screen in pixels\n"
"\n"
"Freezes the screen and shows it full screen. Drag to measure a width and height; hold Shift for a straight line. Ctrl+C copies the size, right-click clears, Esc closes."
msgstr ""
"以像素为单位测量屏幕上的距离\n"
"\n"
"冻结屏幕并全屏显示。拖动可测量宽度和高度；按住 Shift 可画直线。Ctrl+C 复制尺寸，右键清除，Esc 关闭。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Keep the computer from sleeping or locking its screen"
msgstr "阻止电脑休眠或锁定屏幕"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Keep the computer from sleeping or locking its screen\n"
"\n"
"Held by the background service, so it continues after this command or the window closes. Without DURATION, shows whether Keep Awake is on."
msgstr ""
"阻止电脑休眠或锁定屏幕\n"
"\n"
"由后台服务维持，因此在此命令结束或窗口关闭后仍会继续。不带 DURATION 时，显示“保持唤醒”是否已开启。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"30m, 1h, 1h30m or a number of minutes; `on` until turned off; `off` to stop"
msgstr "30m、1h、1h30m 或分钟数；`on` 表示直到关闭；`off` 表示停止"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show which programs keep a file, folder, drive or network port busy"
msgstr "显示哪些程序占用了文件、文件夹、磁盘或网络端口"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Show which programs keep a file, folder, drive or network port busy\n"
"\n"
"TARGET is a path, or a port number such as 3000. Lists each program with its PID and how it uses the target. Only your own programs can be checked as a normal user; run it with sudo to include other users' programs and system services."
msgstr ""
"显示哪些程序占用了文件、文件夹、磁盘或网络端口\n"
"\n"
"TARGET 是路径，或像 3000 这样的端口号。列出每个程序及其 PID，以及它如何使用该目标。普通用户只能检查自己的程序；请用 sudo 运行以包含其他用户的程序和系统服务。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "A file, folder or mount point, or a port number"
msgstr "文件、文件夹或挂载点，或端口号"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Paste the clipboard converted: tidy JSON, a table as Markdown, a cleaned link…"
msgstr "粘贴转换后的剪贴板内容：整理 JSON、将表格转为 Markdown、清理链接……"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Paste the clipboard converted: tidy JSON, a table as Markdown, a cleaned link…\n"
"\n"
"Opens a small window listing the conversions that fit what's on the clipboard, with a preview of each. Enter pastes the chosen one into the app that had focus and restores the clipboard. An image on the clipboard can be pasted as its text (OCR)."
msgstr ""
"粘贴转换后的剪贴板内容：整理 JSON、将表格转为 Markdown、清理链接……\n"
"\n"
"打开一个小窗口，列出适合剪贴板内容的转换方式，并为每种提供预览。按 Enter 会将所选内容粘贴到原先有焦点的应用并恢复剪贴板。剪贴板中的图片可以以其中的文字形式粘贴（OCR）。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Convert text from standard input with one of Smart Paste's conversions"
msgstr "用智能粘贴的某种转换方式转换标准输入中的文本"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Convert text from standard input with one of Smart Paste's conversions\n"
"\n"
"Without CONVERSION, lists them."
msgstr ""
"用智能粘贴的某种转换方式转换标准输入中的文本\n"
"\n"
"不带 CONVERSION 时，列出所有转换方式。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "A conversion such as json, markdown-table, clean-link or snake"
msgstr "某种转换，如 json、markdown-table、clean-link 或 snake"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Describe this computer: hardware, drivers, health and recent changes"
msgstr "描述这台电脑：硬件、驱动、健康状况和最近的变化"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Describe this computer: hardware, drivers, health and recent changes\n"
"\n"
"Prints a report that's safe to share in a forum or bug report (no serial numbers, names or network addresses), with checks and fixes for drivers, drive health, disk space, temperatures and firmware updates. Also saves today's snapshot, so later reports can show what changed."
msgstr ""
"描述这台电脑：硬件、驱动、健康状况和最近的变化\n"
"\n"
"打印一份可以放心分享到论坛或错误报告的报告（不含序列号、名称或网络地址），其中包含对驱动、硬盘健康、磁盘空间、温度和固件更新的检查与修复建议。同时会保存今天的快照，以便之后的报告显示有什么变化。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Also show memory slots and upgrade options (asks for the administrator password)"
msgstr "同时显示内存插槽和升级选项（需要管理员密码）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Explain why the computer doesn't sleep, or why it woke up"
msgstr "说明电脑为什么没有休眠，或为什么被唤醒"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Explain why the computer doesn't sleep, or why it woke up\n"
"\n"
"Shows what keeps the computer awake right now (apps and settings), the sleeps of the last week with what started and ended each one and the battery used, and the USB devices allowed to wake it."
msgstr ""
"说明电脑为什么没有休眠，或为什么被唤醒\n"
"\n"
"显示此刻是什么让电脑保持唤醒（应用和设置）、最近一周的每次休眠及其开始和结束的原因与耗电量，以及允许唤醒电脑的 USB 设备。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Monitor NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics cards and tune their power, fans, clocks and temperature"
msgstr "监控 NVIDIA、AMD 和 Intel 显卡，并调节它们的功耗、风扇、频率和温度"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Monitor NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics cards and tune their power, fans, clocks and temperature\n"
"\n"
"Without a subcommand, shows each card with its readings and which controls it supports, with the reason for any it doesn't. Changing settings needs administrator rights, and anything you don't confirm is undone."
msgstr ""
"监控 NVIDIA、AMD 和 Intel 显卡，并调节它们的功耗、风扇、频率和温度\n"
"\n"
"不带子命令时，显示每块显卡的读数和它支持的控制项，不支持的会说明原因。更改设置需要管理员权限，未经确认的更改都会被撤销。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Show the graphics cards, their readings and what each lets you control"
msgstr "显示显卡、它们的读数以及每块显卡允许控制的内容"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Apply GPU settings from a JSON file, undoing them unless you confirm"
msgstr "从 JSON 文件应用 GPU 设置，未经确认则撤销"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Apply GPU settings from a JSON file, undoing them unless you confirm\n"
"\n"
"The file holds the settings for one card: its PCI address as \"gpu\", and any of \"power_limit_w\", \"fan\" ({\"mode\":\"auto\"}, {\"mode\":\"fixed\",\"speed_pct\":50} or {\"mode\":\"curve\",\"points\":[...]}), \"temperature_target_c\", \"core_offset_mhz\", \"mem_offset_mhz\", \"voltage_offset_mv\", for AMD cards with a full curve \"voltage_curve\" (a list of {\"mhz\":1450,\"mv\":800} points, all of them), and for Intel \"core_clock_min_mhz\" and \"core_clock_max_mhz\". Values the card doesn't allow are refused."
msgstr ""
"从 JSON 文件应用 GPU 设置，未经确认则撤销\n"
"\n"
"文件包含一块显卡的设置：以 \"gpu\" 给出它的 PCI 地址，以及下列任意字段：\"power_limit_w\"、\"fan\"（{\"mode\":\"auto\"}、{\"mode\":\"fixed\",\"speed_pct\":50} 或 {\"mode\":\"curve\",\"points\":[...]}）、\"temperature_target_c\"、\"core_offset_mhz\"、\"mem_offset_mhz\"、\"voltage_offset_mv\"，对有完整曲线的 AMD 显卡还有 \"voltage_curve\"（由 {\"mhz\":1450,\"mv\":800} 这样的点组成的列表，需包含所有点），对 Intel 显卡还有 \"core_clock_min_mhz\" 和 \"core_clock_max_mhz\"。显卡不允许的值会被拒绝。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The settings file, or - to read it from standard input"
msgstr "设置文件，或用 - 从标准输入读取"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Keep the settings after a restart, and run fan curves in the background service"
msgstr "重启后保留设置，并在后台服务中运行风扇曲线"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Keep the settings without asking for confirmation"
msgstr "不经确认直接保留设置"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Seconds to wait for confirmation before undoing the change"
msgstr "撤销更改前等待确认的秒数"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Remove a card's saved settings and give its fans back to the card"
msgstr "删除某块显卡已保存的设置，并把风扇还给显卡"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The card's PCI address, as `voltkit gpu` shows it"
msgstr "显卡的 PCI 地址，与 `voltkit gpu` 显示的一致"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Run the background service that applies saved GPU settings and follows fan curves"
msgstr "运行后台服务，应用已保存的 GPU 设置并执行风扇曲线"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Record the readings of a card for a while, to compare profiles later"
msgstr "录制一块显卡一段时间的读数，以便之后比较配置文件"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Record the readings of a card for a while, to compare profiles later\n"
"\n"
"Writes a CSV file you can open in a spreadsheet, and prints a summary with the energy used and the clock-work each watt bought (\"active MHz per watt\"). Run it while a game or a benchmark is going, once per profile, then compare the sessions."
msgstr ""
"录制一块显卡一段时间的读数，以便之后比较配置文件\n"
"\n"
"写出一个可在电子表格中打开的 CSV 文件，并输出摘要，包含耗电量以及每瓦换来的频率工作量（“每瓦有效频率”）。请在游戏或基准测试运行时，为每个配置文件各运行一次，然后比较这些会话。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "How many seconds to record"
msgstr "录制多少秒"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "What is being tried, such as the profile name"
msgstr "正在测试什么，例如配置文件的名称"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The card's PCI address (the first NVIDIA or AMD card by default)"
msgstr "显卡的 PCI 地址（默认是第一块 NVIDIA 或 AMD 显卡）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Check Voltkit's readings against a second source and measure what monitoring costs"
msgstr "用第二个数据源核对 Voltkit 的读数，并测量监控的开销"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Check Voltkit's readings against a second source and measure what monitoring costs\n"
"\n"
"On NVIDIA cards it compares NVML, which Voltkit reads, with `nvidia-smi` taken at the same moments, and reports how far apart they are against the accuracy targets. It also measures the CPU time and memory monitoring uses. Cards from other makers have no second source on most computers; the command says so."
msgstr ""
"用第二个数据源核对 Voltkit 的读数，并测量监控的开销\n"
"\n"
"对 NVIDIA 显卡，它会把 Voltkit 所读取的 NVML 与同一时刻的 `nvidia-smi` 进行对比，并对照精度目标报告两者的差距。它还会测量监控所用的 CPU 时间和内存。在大多数电脑上，其他厂商的显卡没有第二个数据源，命令会说明这一点。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "How many seconds to compare for"
msgstr "对比多少秒"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "List the recorded sessions, newest first"
msgstr "列出已录制的会话，最新的在前"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Compare two recorded sessions side by side"
msgstr "并排比较两次已录制的会话"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Compare two recorded sessions side by side\n"
"\n"
"Each session is a file, or a number from `voltkit gpu sessions`. Shows temperature, power, energy, fan speed, clocks and efficiency, and which session is better at each. Efficiency is \"active MHz per watt\", a proxy for work per watt; add an fps column from a tool such as MangoHud to a session file to get frames per second per watt too."
msgstr ""
"并排比较两次已录制的会话\n"
"\n"
"每个会话是一个文件，或是 `voltkit gpu sessions` 列出的编号。会显示温度、功耗、耗电量、风扇转速、频率和效率，以及每一项中哪次会话更好。效率是“每瓦有效频率”，是每瓦工作量的近似指标；把 MangoHud 等工具得到的 fps 列添加到会话文件中，还能得到每瓦帧数。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The first session"
msgstr "第一次会话"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The second session"
msgstr "第二次会话"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Find out why the video memory stays at a high clock while the card is idle"
msgstr "查明显卡空闲时显存为何停留在高频"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Find out why the video memory stays at a high clock while the card is idle\n"
"\n"
"A common Linux problem: with several monitors, mixed refresh rates or a very fast panel, the driver can't lower the memory clock, and the card draws extra power for nothing. Run it while the desktop is quiet; it reads the clocks and the displays and names the likely causes."
msgstr ""
"查明显卡空闲时显存为何停留在高频\n"
"\n"
"Linux 上的常见问题：使用多个显示器、混合刷新率或超快面板时，驱动无法降低显存频率，显卡会白白多耗电。请在桌面空闲时运行；它会读取频率和显示器，并指出可能的原因。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Suggest the power limit that saves the most power for almost the same speed"
msgstr "建议在速度几乎不变的情况下最省电的功率上限"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Suggest the power limit that saves the most power for almost the same speed\n"
"\n"
"Reads the sessions you recorded under different power limits (`voltkit gpu record`, once per limit, with the same game or benchmark) and picks the lowest limit that stays within the tolerance of the fastest. It only suggests limits you actually measured."
msgstr ""
"建议在速度几乎不变的情况下最省电的功率上限\n"
"\n"
"读取你在不同功率上限下录制的会话（`voltkit gpu record`，每个上限一次，使用同一个游戏或基准测试），并选出在最快者容差范围内最低的上限。它只建议你实际测量过的上限。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "How much slower than the fastest limit is acceptable, in percent"
msgstr "比最快上限慢多少是可以接受的，以百分比计"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Only the sessions of this card (its PCI address)"
msgstr "仅此显卡的会话（其 PCI 地址）"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Named profiles that switch automatically by power source, running app, load or temperature"
msgstr "按电源、运行的应用、负载或温度自动切换的命名配置文件"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "List the saved profiles and the rules that switch between them"
msgstr "列出已保存的配置文件以及在它们之间切换的规则"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show which profile each card is using now"
msgstr "显示每块显卡当前使用的配置文件"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Install profiles and rules from a JSON file, replacing the saved ones"
msgstr "从 JSON 文件安装配置文件和规则，替换已保存的内容"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Install profiles and rules from a JSON file, replacing the saved ones\n"
"\n"
"The file is a list with one entry per card: its PCI address as \"gpu\", its \"profiles\" (each a \"name\" and the same \"settings\" `voltkit gpu apply` takes), its \"rules\" (a \"profile\" and \"conditions\" such as {\"when\":\"power_source\",\"on_battery\":true}, {\"when\":\"app\",\"names\":[\"steam\"]}, {\"when\":\"workload\",\"util_above_pct\":80,\"for_secs\":30} or {\"when\":\"temperature\",\"above_c\":85}) and a \"default\" profile. Rules are tried in order."
msgstr ""
"从 JSON 文件安装配置文件和规则，替换已保存的内容\n"
"\n"
"文件是一个列表，每块显卡一项：以 \"gpu\" 给出它的 PCI 地址，其 \"profiles\"（每个包含 \"name\" 以及与 `voltkit gpu apply` 相同的 \"settings\"），其 \"rules\"（一个 \"profile\" 和 \"conditions\"，如 {\"when\":\"power_source\",\"on_battery\":true}、{\"when\":\"app\",\"names\":[\"steam\"]}、{\"when\":\"workload\",\"util_above_pct\":80,\"for_secs\":30} 或 {\"when\":\"temperature\",\"above_c\":85}），以及一个 \"default\" 配置文件。规则会按顺序逐条尝试。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The profiles file, or - to read it from standard input"
msgstr "配置文件，或用 - 从标准输入读取"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Read QR codes from the screen or image files, or make them from text"
msgstr "从屏幕或图片文件读取二维码，或由文字生成二维码"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Select a screen region and copy the text of the QR code in it"
msgstr "选取屏幕区域，并复制其中二维码的文字"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Print the text of every QR code in an image file"
msgstr "打印图片文件中每个二维码的文字"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show TEXT as a QR code in the terminal, or save it as a PNG image"
msgstr "在终端中将 TEXT 显示为二维码，或将其保存为 PNG 图片"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Save a PNG image instead of printing to the terminal"
msgstr "保存为 PNG 图片，而不是在终端中打印"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Put a small logo (PNG, JPEG, WebP or SVG) in the middle of the code (PNG output only). The code is read back to make sure it still scans"
msgstr "在二维码中间放置一个小标志（PNG、JPEG、WebP 或 SVG）（仅限 PNG 输出）。生成后会回读二维码，确保仍可扫描"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Run the background service that listens for global shortcuts"
msgstr "运行监听全局快捷键的后台服务"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Run the background service that listens for global shortcuts\n"
"\n"
"Without a subcommand, runs the service in the foreground until interrupted. It owns io.github.arios4k.Voltkit.Daemon on the session bus, so only one instance runs, and binds the configured hotkeys through the XDG GlobalShortcuts portal when the desktop provides it."
msgstr ""
"运行监听全局快捷键的后台服务\n"
"\n"
"不带子命令时，在前台运行该服务直到被中断。它在会话总线上拥有 io.github.arios4k.Voltkit.Daemon，因此只会运行一个实例；当桌面提供 XDG GlobalShortcuts 门户时，通过它绑定已配置的快捷键。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show whether the daemon is running and how shortcuts are bound"
msgstr "显示守护进程是否在运行，以及快捷键是如何绑定的"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Stop the running daemon"
msgstr "停止正在运行的守护进程"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Make the running daemon re-read snippets from the config file"
msgstr "让正在运行的守护进程重新读取配置文件中的片段"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Start the daemon automatically at login"
msgstr "登录时自动启动守护进程"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Stop starting the daemon at login"
msgstr "不再在登录时启动守护进程"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Check that everything Voltkit needs is installed and set up"
msgstr "检查 Voltkit 所需的一切是否已安装并配置好"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Check that everything Voltkit needs is installed and set up\n"
"\n"
"Checks the helper programs, OCR language data, desktop portals, clipboard tools, the background service and hotkeys, then prints the install command for anything missing on this distro."
msgstr ""
"检查 Voltkit 所需的一切是否已安装并配置好\n"
"\n"
"检查辅助程序、OCR 语言数据、桌面门户、剪贴板工具、后台服务和快捷键，然后打印在此发行版上安装缺失项的命令。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn't running"
msgstr "通过守护进程运行某个快捷键操作；如果它没有运行，则直接运行"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn't running\n"
"\n"
"Meant to be bound to a key in the desktop's keyboard settings or a compositor config. Results and errors are shown as desktop notifications."
msgstr ""
"通过守护进程运行某个快捷键操作；如果它没有运行，则直接运行\n"
"\n"
"用于绑定到桌面键盘设置或合成器配置中的某个按键。结果和错误会以桌面通知的形式显示。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal"
msgstr "为没有 GlobalShortcuts 门户的桌面管理 GNOME 快捷键"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Manage GNOME keybindings for desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal\n"
"\n"
"Adds or removes custom shortcuts in GNOME Settings (via gsettings) that run `voltkit trigger`. Other custom shortcuts are left untouched."
msgstr ""
"为没有 GlobalShortcuts 门户的桌面管理 GNOME 快捷键\n"
"\n"
"在 GNOME 设置中添加或移除运行 `voltkit trigger` 的自定义快捷键（通过 gsettings）。其他自定义快捷键不受影响。"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Add Super+Shift+T, C and E (or your configured keys) to GNOME Settings"
msgstr "将 Super+Shift+T、C 和 E（或你配置的按键）添加到 GNOME 设置"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Print the gsettings commands instead of running them"
msgstr "打印 gsettings 命令，而不是运行它们"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Remove the keybindings added by `install`"
msgstr "移除由 `install` 添加的快捷键"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "List every system-wide shortcut, grouped by who owns it"
msgstr "列出所有系统级快捷键，按所有者分组"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid ""
"Show what a shortcut does, such as `voltkit shortcuts who super+shift+s`"
msgstr "显示某个快捷键的作用，如 `voltkit shortcuts who super+shift+s`"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "The keys, like super+shift+s, ctrl+alt+t or print"
msgstr "按键，如 super+shift+s、ctrl+alt+t 或 print"

#: src/main.rs (command-line help)
msgid "Show shortcuts used by more than one action"
msgstr "显示被多个操作使用的快捷键"
